{"timestamp":"2026-09-16T21:16:22.401Z","event":"run_completed","version":"v3","workflowStatus":"success","workspace":{"id":"RET01-2026-09-16T21-15-48-447Z","root":"/Users/i.kohanvs/Desktop/ai-native/.worktrees/RET01-2026-09-16T21-15-48-447Z","baseRevision":"3e10b5b4c3fa167a1fb4e02a6715cb9795c4ff45","ref":"HEAD"},"specDecision":"executable","spec":{"goal":"Update task completion lifecycle behavior so completed tasks expose a completion timestamp and reopened tasks clear it.","requirements":["In `TaskService.complete`, when an existing task is completed, set `completedAt` to a generated timestamp string while setting status to `completed`.","In `TaskService.reopen`, when an existing task is reopened, set status to `pending` and `completedAt` to `null`.","Preserve existing not-found behavior and route response shapes for complete and reopen operations.","Keep newly created tasks pending with `completedAt: null`."],"constraints":["`Task.completedAt` is typed as `string | null`; use a serialized timestamp string compatible with that type (an ISO 8601 string is the repository-consistent implementation choice).","Changes should be limited to the task lifecycle behavior; no API routing or unrelated task behavior changes are needed.","Do not alter the existing 404 responses for unknown task IDs."],"nonGoals":["Changing task creation, listing, filtering, title validation, or ID generation.","Changing the HTTP methods, paths, status codes, or response envelopes.","Defining persistence beyond the in-memory `TaskService` already used by the app."],"acceptance":["Completing an existing pending task returns status `200`, status `completed`, and a non-empty timestamp string in `completedAt`.","The completed task retains that `completedAt` value when read through the service/API until it is reopened.","Reopening a completed task returns status `200`, status `pending`, and `completedAt: null`.","The reopened task also has `completedAt: null` when subsequently read or listed.","Unknown task IDs continue to return `404` with `{ error: \"task_not_found\" }`.","Existing task tests pass, including the completion and reopen cases in `tests/tasks.test.ts`."],"verification":["Run the repository test script: `npm test`.","Confirm the existing `complete and reopen` tests pass.","If adding or extending tests, cover completion timestamp presence, reopening clearing the field, and persistence of both resulting values through subsequent reads/listing."],"ambiguities":[{"question":"What timestamp serialization should be used for `completedAt`?","classification":"safe_inference","status":"resolved","resolution":"Use `new Date().toISOString()` (or equivalent ISO 8601 serialization), yielding the required string timestamp while matching the existing `string | null` type.","basis":"The task requires a timestamp, `Task.completedAt` is typed as `string | null`, and the existing tests require a non-empty string but impose no more specific format; ISO 8601 is the standard low-risk representation."},{"question":"What should happen if the complete endpoint is called for a task that is already completed?","classification":"safe_inference","status":"resolved","resolution":"The required behavior is the pending-to-completed transition; no additional product rule is needed for repeated completion calls. Implement the stated transition and do not change unrelated lifecycle semantics.","basis":"The task wording specifies behavior when a task becomes completed, and the repository only tests the pending-to-completed transition; this change request does not define repeated-completion semantics."}]},"specPath":"/Users/i.kohanvs/Desktop/ai-native/traces/RET01-2026-09-16T21-15-48-447Z-C.spec.json","implementationStarted":false,"failureReason":null,"unresolvedQuestions":[],"turns":0,"modelCalls":1,"toolCalls":1,"specModelCalls":0,"specToolCalls":0,"planningEnabled":false,"plan":null,"plannerModelCalls":0,"plannerToolCalls":0,"plannerDurationMs":0,"subagentsEnabled":false,"reviewPla